# Fixed defect 267, 2026-10-04 (lane b11-parse), the parser's half. Symptom:
# reading a declaration of N members took work that grew with N squared:
# `parse` over a clean record of 8,000 fields retired 5.37 billion
# instructions against 0.63 at 2,000, a variant's cases, a case's fields, a
# generic record's and a commented record's the same, and a record whose
# fields each end with a `,` 17.0 billion. Causes, found with `sample`: each
# member was pushed with a `.must()` inside the push, which kept the push
# from growing the array in place (`parse/member_lines.fields_of`,
# `case_block`); a case's fields in braces below it were pushed through
# `cases[last]`, and each `,`'s deletion into its report through
# `c.diagnostics[habit]`, places no push grows in place. Each push copied
# every member before it. Repair: each member is matched out before its
# push, and the other two grow in a local stored once; 8,000 fields now
# retire 1.29 billion, and the `,` record 2.10. Nothing said moves: this
# case pins each shape's messages and fixes, as before. The resolver's half,
# a record's field names kept in a table copied at each name, is not this
# repair's (`resolve/state.keyed_add`).

record Point
    x: i64  #~ expected_end_of_line
    y: i64
    # a doc comment above the last field
    z: i64

variant Shape
    dot
    circle
    {  #~ expected_case
        r: i64
        d: i64
    }

variant Plain
    one
    two
        a: i64
        b: i64

function main()
    p = Point(x: 1, y: 2, z: 3)
    print(p.x)
